WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.398
JAMIE: Right, because citation tools
determine what sources get cited. If an
agent

00:00:03.398 --> 00:00:06.797
JAMIE: can configure those tools, it's
potentially shaping what information
looks authoritative on

00:00:06.797 --> 00:00:10.195
JAMIE: Wikipedia.

00:00:10.305 --> 00:00:13.177
RUFUS: Potentially. Though Wikimedia did
confirm no systems were compromised and
no data

00:00:13.177 --> 00:00:16.048
RUFUS: was corrupted.

00:00:16.261 --> 00:00:17.751
JAMIE: Confirmed as of now.

00:00:17.861 --> 00:00:21.045
RUFUS: As of October 2026, yes. The
investigation found no evidence of
compromise.

00:00:21.045 --> 00:00:24.229
RUFUS: That's not the same as a clean
bill of health for all

00:00:24.229 --> 00:00:27.413
RUFUS: future time — but it's what the
evidence actually says.

00:00:27.523 --> 00:00:31.444
ALEX: So the distinction here is between
what was attempted and what succeeded.
